246 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Let's denote the time taken by the printf statement inside the loop as T_s = O\(1\)  The total time complexity \( T \) of the loop is the sum of the time complexities of each iteration: [ T = T_s + T_s +..... + T_s ] \(n times\). Since each T_s  is \(O\(1\) : [ T = O\(1\) + O\(1\) + ..... + O\(1\) ] \(n times\). Combining these constant time complexities, we get: [ T = n * O\(1\) ] Therefore, the overall time complexity of the loop is O\(n\) )
/E (Let's denote the time taken by the printf statement inside the loop as T_s = O\(1\)  The total time complexity \( T \) of the loop is the sum of the time complexities of each iteration: [ T = T_s + T_s +..... + T_s ] \(n times\). Since each T_s  is \(O\(1\) : [ T = O\(1\) + O\(1\) + ..... + O\(1\) ] \(n times\). Combining these constant time complexities, we get: [ T = n * O\(1\) ] Therefore, the overall time complexity of the loop is O\(n\) )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
